#SOC teams are divided into different tiers to respond to incidents and keep data safe.

#Tier 1 is the filter for the rest of the team. They respond to alerts and verify if it needs escalation or can be handled at that level.

#Tier 2 is the more experienced filter. They can handle a broader range of incidents and respond appropriately to them. If Tier 2 notices that an event
#happened that may require deeper investigation and immediate response, IR can be called in.

#IR handles everything from incident handling, forensics, and cross-team communication.

#The ultimate goal is to keep the data safe!

#SOC L1s need to know the importance of writing reports:

#Clear reports save time for L2 analysts and help them know what happened.

#Reports can save SIEM findings for records.

#Writing reports helps the L1 analyst better understand what they’re doing.

#Five W’s: Who, What, When, Where, Why

